# Before writing or changing music, read music/README.md (style, moods, format).
# The main menu's song (src/game/menu.js), after the splash screen's glass bird has broken. It grew
# out of a test of the Westworld theme on glass: a kid plays with a glass bird, and it shatters. Westworld's scale (A minor, with its Bb and
# G#), pulse (6/8, a dotted quarter at 67) and glass. The bird's own sound is the end of Westworld:
# a grace note falling onto two notes a step apart, ringing. Whole, the step is wide (A+B); as the
# bird cracks it narrows (A+Bb). The toy tune fades as the bird cracks, and the break follows the
# splash screen (src/audio/splash.js): a knock, a thin ring held while time stands still, the
# shatter, a low swell onto D (an open fifth here: no F#, the scale stays). The shards ring over D,
# then E leads back to the start.
title    The Glass Bird
composer Claude
about    A kid and a glass bird, in A minor and 6/8, played on glass. Alone: a rocking crystal ostinato, a singing bowl and a glass heartbeat, the bird calling (a grace note falling onto two notes a step apart). Playing: a toy tune on crystal, like a nursery song, opening on the game's motif (A B C E D). Flying: a turn to C major, the bird answering the tune in its held notes, climbing and twice singing it back; back in minor its answers fall, shorten and break off. Cracking: Bb creeps into the ostinato, the call narrows to a half step, the tune loses more each time until only a ghost of it is left on the glass harmonica, and the bass sinks. Then the break as on the splash screen: a knock and a thin glass ring while everything stands still, the shatter, glass falling and slowing, a low swell onto D. Over D the bird's calls ring in pieces, without the tune, and E leads back to the start. Only the main menu plays it, so it only knows explore.
tempo    67       # a dotted quarter
beats    2
steps    6        # 6/8 in sixteenths: 12 steps a bar
reverb   0.45

# moods (music/README.md); the main menu only ever plays explore
# mood explore: lead glow bird wing arp ost haze bowl tap chimes break knock ring swell bass

voice lead    crystal    vol=0.85 pan=-0.1
voice glow    glassharp  vol=0.3  pan=0.2  att=0.06 rel=0.4
voice bird    crystal    vol=0.55 pan=0.4  rev=0.7
voice wing    crystal    vol=0.42 pan=0.35 rev=0.6
voice arp     crystal    vol=0.3  pan=0.3
voice ost     crystal    vol=0.45 pan=-0.3 oct=1
voice haze    glassharp  vol=0.16 pan=-0.2 att=0.8 rel=1.2
voice bowl    bowl       vol=0.28 pan=0.1  rev=0.6
voice tap     glasstap   vol=0.22 pan=0.35
voice chimes  chimes     vol=0.3  pan=-0.4
voice break   shatter    vol=0.6
voice knock   kick       vol=0.35
voice ring    glassharp  vol=0.14 pan=0.3  rev=0.8 att=0.15 rel=1.2
voice swell   glassharp  vol=0.3  pan=-0.1 att=1.2 rel=1.5
voice bass    fretless   vol=0.7  glide=0.08

# Alone (8 bars): the ostinato rocks on its root and the step above it (the bird's interval),
# a glass heartbeat, and the bird calls into the rest bars. Am Am F F Am Am G E
pattern alone
ost    | A2!- A2- B2- A2!- A2- B2- | % | F2!- F2- G2- F2!- F2- G2- | % | A2!- A2- B2- A2!- A2- B2- | % | G2!- G2- A2- G2!- G2- A2- | E2!- E2- F2- E2!- E2- F2- |
bowl   | A3----------- | _ | F3----------- | _ | A3----------- | _ | G3----------- | E3----------- |
tap    | x.o... ...... | _ | x.o... ...... | _ | x.o... ...... | _ | x.o... ...... | x.o... ...... |
bird   | _ | _ | _ | A6 A5+B5---------- | _ | _ | _ | .----- A6 A5+B5---- |
bass   | A1----------- | % | F1----------- | % | C2----------- | % | B1----------- | G#1----------- |
lead   | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ |

# Playing (16 bars): the toy tune, quarter and eighth like a nursery song.
# Am Am F F Am Am G E | F F Dm Dm Bb Bb Am Am
pattern play1
lead   | A4--- B4- C5----- | E5----- D5----- | C5----------- | .----------- | A4--- B4- C5----- | E5----- G5----- | F5--- E5- D5----- | E5----------- |
bird   | _ | _ | _ | A6 A5+B5---------- | _ | _ | _ | .----- E6 D5+E5---- |
ost    | A2!- A2- B2- A2!- A2- B2- | % | F2!- F2- G2- F2!- F2- G2- | % | A2!- A2- B2- A2!- A2- B2- | % | G2!- G2- A2- G2!- G2- A2- | E2!- E2- F2- E2!- E2- F2- |
bowl   | A3----------- | _ | F3----------- | _ | A3----------- | _ | G3----------- | E3----------- |
tap    | x.o... ...... | _ | x.o... ...... | _ | x.o... ...... | _ | x.o... ...... | _ |
bass   | C2----- A1----- | C2----- B1----- | A1----------- | F1----------- | C2----- A1----- | C2----- E2----- | D2----- B1----- | G#1----------- |

pattern play2
lead   | .----- C5--- D5- | E5--- D5- C5----- | D5--- C5- A4----- | .----------- | .----- D5--- C5- | Bb4----------- | A4----------- | .----------- |
bird   | _ | _ | _ | A6 A5+B5---------- | _ | _ | _ | A6 A5+B5---------- |
ost    | F2!- F2- G2- F2!- F2- G2- | % | D2!- D2- E2- D2!- D2- E2- | % | Bb2!- Bb2- C3- Bb2!- Bb2- C3- | % | A2!- A2- B2- A2!- A2- B2- | % |
bowl   | F3----------- | _ | D3----------- | _ | Bb3----------- | _ | A3----------- | _ |
tap    | x.o... ...... | _ | x.o... ...... | _ | x.o... ...... | _ | x.o... ...... | _ |
bass   | F1----- A1----- | C2----- A1----- | F1----------- | D2----------- | Bb1----- A1----- | G1----------- | C2----------- | A1----------- |

# Flying (16 bars): the tune, broken chords below, a turn to C major for a while. The
# bird answers the kid in the tune's held notes and keeps quiet while it moves: a few quick wing
# beats (often a trill on its own step) and a note that rings on, each answer higher than the last
# and never the same length twice; twice it sings the toy tune's motif (A B C E D) back, fast. Back
# in minor (fly2) the answers fall and get shorter, and the last one breaks off.
# Without doubling: the glass harmonica sits out the flight.
pattern fly1
lead   | C5--- E5- G5----- | A5--- G5- E5----- | D5--- G5- B5----- | A5----- G5----- | A5--- C6- A5--- F5- | G5----- E5----- | B5----- G#5----- | E5----------- |
wing   | .----- A5 B5 A5 B5 E6- | .----- B5 C6 E6 G6-- | .----- D6 E6 D6 B6-- | .------- G6 A6 D7- | _ | .----- A5 B5 C6 E6 D6- | .----- G#5 B5 E6 G#6 B6- | E7 B6 G#6 E6-- .----- |
ost    | C2- G2- E3- G2- E3- G2- | % | G2- D3- B3- D3- B3- D3- | % | F2- C3- A3- C3- A3- C3- | % | E2- B2- G#3- B2- G#3- B2- | % |
bowl   | C3----------- | _ | G3----------- | _ | F3----------- | _ | E3----------- | _ |
bird   | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | .----- A6 A5+B5---- |
bass   | E2----- C2----- | F2----- C2----- | B1----- G1----- | C2----- B1----- | F1----- A1----- | C2----------- | G#1----- E1----- | G#1----------- |

pattern fly2
lead   | C6--- B5- A5----- | E5----- A5----- | C6--- B5- A5--- G5- | A5----------- | F5--- E5- D5----- | A5----- F5----- | E5----------- | .----------- |
wing   | .----- C7 B6 A6 E6-- | .----- B6 A6 B6 E6-- | _ | .- A5 B5 C6 E6 D6----- | .----- A5 G5 F5--- | .------- E6 D6-- | .----- A5 B5 A5 .-- | _ |
ost    | A2- E3- A3- E3- A3- E3- | % | F2- C3- A3- C3- A3- C3- | % | D2- A2- F3- A2- F3- A2- | % | E2- B2- G#3- B2- G#3- B2- | % |
bowl   | A3----------- | _ | F3----------- | _ | D3----------- | _ | E3----------- | _ |
bird   | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | A6 A5+B5---------- |
bass   | A1----- C2----- | C2----------- | A1----- F1----- | C2----------- | D2----- Bb1----- | F1----- D2----- | G#1----------- | E1----------- |

# Cracking (12 bars): Bb creeps into the ostinato, the call narrows from A+B to A+Bb, and the
# tune fades: it loses its D, then half of itself, then all but its first note, with a ghost of it
# on the glass harmonica; a cluster hangs; the heart skips; the bass sinks a half step a bar.
# Then the knock, and a thin ring while everything stands still (as on the splash screen).
# Am Am F F Am Am Bb Bb Am Am (knock) (still)
pattern crack
lead   | A4--- B4- C5----- | E5----- .----- | _ | _ | A4--- B4- .----- | _ | _ | _ | A4----- .----- | _ | _ | _ |
glow   | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | .----- C4----- | _ | _ | .----- Bb3----- | _ | _ | _ |
bird   | _ | _ | A6 A5+B5---------- | .----- A5+Bb5?----- | _ | _ | _ | A6 A5+Bb5---------- | _ | A6! A5+Bb5!---------- | _ | _ |
haze   | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | A4+Bb4----------- | = | = | _ | A4+Bb4+E5----------- | _ | _ |
ost    | A2!- A2- B2- A2!- A2- B2- | % | F2!- F2- G2- F2!- F2- G2- | % | A2!- A2- Bb2- A2!- A2- B2- | A2!- A2- Bb2- A2!- A2- Bb2- | Bb2!- Bb2- B2- Bb2!- .- B2- | Bb2!- .- B2- Bb2!- .- .- | A2!- .- Bb2- A2!- A2- .- | A2!- .- .- A2!- .- Bb2- | _ | _ |
bowl   | A3----------- | _ | F3----------- | _ | A3----------- | _ | Bb2----------- | _ | A3----------- | _ | _ | _ |
tap    | x.o... ...... | ...... x.o... | ....x. ...... | x..... ..o... | x.o... ...... | ..x.o. ...... | x..... x..... | ...... ....x. | x.o.x. ...... | X..... ...... | _ | _ |
knock  | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | X..... ...... | _ |
ring   | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | G6----------- | = |
bass   | C2----- A1----- | C2----------- | A1----------- | F1----------- | C2----------- | B1----------- | Bb1----------- | A1----------- | Ab1----------- | G1----------- | D1!- .--------- | _ |

# The shatter and the shards (12 bars): the break, two showers of glass falling and slowing,
# a low swell onto D and A; then over D the bird's wide calls in pieces, never in the same place
# or octave, and no tune; E in the bass leads back to the start.
pattern shatter
break  | X..... ...... | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ |
chimes | x..x.. x..... | ...... ..x... | ....x. ...... | _ | _ | x..... ...... | _ | _ | _ | ...... x..... | _ | _ |
lead   | E7! B6? A6 F6? D6 Bb5? G5 E5? C5 A4? F4 D4? | C6?- G5- E5?- B4- A4?- E4- | B5?--- F5?--- C5?--- | A4?----- .----- | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ |
arp    | .- C7 G6 E6? B5 A5? F5 D5? B4 G4? E4 | .- A6?- E6- C6?- G5- D5?- | .--- E6?--- A5?--- | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ |
swell  | _ | D2+A2+D3+A3----------- | = | = | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ | _ |
bird   | _ | _ | _ | _ | .----- E6 D5+E5---- | A6 A5+B5---------- | _ | .--- D7 G5+A5------ | C7 C6+D6---------- | .------- A6 D5+E5-- | _ | A6 A5+B5---------- |
ost    | _ | _ | _ | _ | D2!----------- | = | = | = | D2!----------- | = | = | = |
bowl   | _ | D3----------- | _ | _ | D3----------- | _ | _ | _ | D3----------- | _ | _ | _ |
bass   | _ | D1----------- | = | = | D2----------- | = | F1----------- | = | A1----------- | = | E1----------- | = |

loop alone play1 play2 fly1 fly2 crack shatter
